<title>SWITZERLAND: BZ Bank 1996 profit drops with zero extra income.</title>
<headline>BZ Bank 1996 profit drops with zero extra income.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996:</p>
<p>				   (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net profit	     106.8	     vs 185.5</p>
<p> Return on equity (ROE) pct 42		  vs 63</p>
<p> Gross profit		   152.4	     vs 170.5</p>
<p> Extraordinary income	 zero		vs 89.6</p>
<p> Taxes			    42.8		vs 74.0</p>
<p> Net interest income	  19.4		vs 8.6</p>
<p> Commission income	    127.2	     vs 129.9</p>
<p> Trading result		 11.0		vs 38.4</p>
<p> Administrative expenses    6.1		 vs 6.4</p>
<p> Group assets		   754.4	     vs 719.3</p>
<p> Securities trade portfolio 237.3	     vs 201.5</p>
<p> Financial investments	25.3		vs 45.2</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name is BZ Bank Zurich AG, a 100-percent subsidiary of the BZ Group Holding.</p>
<p>In 1995 BZ Bank reduced its trading portfolio and realised extraordinary income on the sale of securities. This was not the case in 1996. The trading portfolio was cut to reduce volatility of earnings and because of the taxes that are paid on capital gains, BZ Bank's president Martin Ebner told a news conference.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom 41-1-631 7340</p>
</text>
